.TH DANBY-CHILDCARE 1
.SH NAME
danby-childcare \- stage-structured predator-prey model with parental care
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B danby/childcare
.SH MODEL
P' = rP-H;
J' = cH-(m+dJ(1-0.8u))J;
A' = mJ-dA A;
.PP
H=a(1-0.6u)PA is predation, P is prey, J young predators, A adult predators,
and u is parental-care effort.  Care reduces juvenile mortality but also
reduces adult hunting, making the biological tradeoff explicit.  The
three-state system cannot be represented faithfully by a two-axis population
phase portrait.
.SH DISPLAY
The history plot gives prey, young, and adult populations separate traces.
The adjacent labelled bars show their instantaneous magnitudes and can be
dragged to change the state directly.  This exposes the maturation delay
between food intake, young predators, and hunting adults.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag a state bar to change that population.  The seven bottom tracks set prey
birth, attack, conversion, maturation, young and adult death, and care effort.
Space pauses, period steps, r resets, and q exits.
.SH NUMERICS
The equation module is
.B /appl/danby/plugin/childcare.b
and the reusable N-state interface is
.B /module/danby/populationmodel.m.
The empty-population boundary and model metadata are regression-tested by
.B temple/danbytest.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/childcare.b
.br
.B /appl/temple/populations.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR danby-ecology (1),
.IR numerics (2)
